  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe Part section omits two controls that already ship.\n\n- Add the Passes rows `The part is` and `Back stock`, with their defaults.\n- Explain `Cut-off piece`, `Chuck piece`, the scrap side, and the back-stock offset.\n- Record the documentation decision. The adjacent turning sections need no change.\n\n## Source checks\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/turning_page.rs:298–314`: tab, labels, choices, and hints.\n- `crates/motion/src/turning/parting_law.rs:84–132`: defaults, scrap side, and flank offset.\n- PR #3503 is merged. These controls are present on `main`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Focused documentation assertions: failed on the base for the missing row; passed with this change.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: exit 0, zero steps. No Rust tests ran.\n- `test_guide_icons.GuideIcons.test_operation_sections_and_guide_components_match_app`: passed.\n- `test_operation_reference.OperationReferencePictures.test_every_operation_has_section_and_picture`: failed on the existing `RotaryFlow` coverage gap. The unchanged baseline fails at the same enum comparison, before reading the guide.\n- Checked the adjacent turning sections. No second Part settings table has this gap.\n\n## Limits\n\nThis PR changes documentation only. It changes no toolpath, UI, post, or machine behavior.\nZola is not installed, so site rendering tests did not run.\nThe global light lane did not run under this contribution's explicit no-rebuild scope. It is not reported as passed.\nNo application build, catalog suite, GUI test, or physical-machine test ran.\nThe contributor claim uses an issue comment. This account cannot set repository labels or assignments.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #3680\n",
